      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Classifies one identity from its before and after heads: a head only after counts +1, a head only before counts −1, and a successor whose compared content differs counts once on each side. A successor with identical content but different realizations or members is tallied attached-only outside +/−, while an unchanged head with unchanged attachments tallies nothing. When either side has no single head, the identity counts as unresolved only if the two sides' head sets differ, and otherwise tallies nothing.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "d329c4f45719a62978a732785750f147d6e2e098",
        "content": "sha256:d377a0c3a0203f4c6de93667d2795a6fa494d9e0dba3f4697ba7974f7481fdf1",
        "locator": {
